      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel exhausted after spending a decade giving everything you had, even when the unexpected result leaves you uncertain about the future. Many people experience this \"midlife peak\" or professional plateau where the immediate goals are met, but the deeper sense of purpose remains unclear, leading to a feeling of aimlessness. Please remember that professional help is a sign of strength, not weakness, and talking about these heavy feelings with a licensed mental health professional can provide a safe space to explore your values and find meaning beyond this specific office.",
      "source": "target",
